  "notes": "Reed / sedge clump ~0.9 m: 18 tapered blades (roots sheath into the base) from three sub-tufts inside a compact 0.3 x 0.4 m curved root strip (not a disc), unequal heights 0.42-0.80 m, each blade splayed 4-10 deg away from its sub-tuft so the clump fans into a V, most leaning the same way (~10-20 deg chord) with tips curving (bend capped per joint, no elbows); 3 thicker stalks with brown cattail-style seed heads (M_solid). Green reed body, short blend to reed_tip over the top third, two dry straw blades as the only pale accents. Roots start 4 cm below y=0 (embed_depth); place at the waterline, the lowest 0.1-0.2 m may sit under water. Custom normals 60% toward +Z, blade front faces the upper (inner) side. Flex 0 at the roots, 1 at the tips."
